  "answer": "Mutual funds must publish their Net Asset Value (NAV) daily. The NAV should be published in at least two daily newspapers (8.1.1). For all schemes except Fund of Fund schemes, the NAV and sale/repurchase price must be updated on AMFI’s website and the Mutual Fund’s own websites by 9 p.m. on the same day (8.1.2). Fund of Fund schemes have an extended deadline: the NAV can be published up to 10 a.m. the following business day, and the NAVs should be published in newspapers with an asterisk to indicate the one‑day lag (8.1.3)."
